    {"type": "global", "symbol": ".data", "disp": 2592, "window": "CRIME", "label": "mvp.o data +0xa20 (CRIME base)", "binaries": ["usr/cpu/sysgen/IP32boot/mvp.o"], "why": "the word at data +0xa20 is 0xb4000000, the KSEG1 address of the CRIME registers, which the video interrupt routines read the interrupt status and mask through (docs/mace-video.md, Driver access)"},
    {"type": "field", "disp": 192, "window": "MACEVCH", "label": "video record +192 (channel from the path)", "binaries": ["usr/cpu/sysgen/IP32boot/mvp.o"], "functions": ["mvptransfer_start_dma", "mvptransfer_stop_dma", "mvptransfer_enablechannel", "mvpinterrupt_clear", "mvpreg_initmace", "mvpreg_syncpath_controls"], "loads": ["lw"], "why": "the video driver's controller record holds one KSEG1 register-set pointer per MACE video channel at +192 + 4 * channel (input 1, input 2, output); mvpreg_init stores 0xbf100000, 0xbf180000 and 0xbf200000 there. These routines index it with a channel number taken from the path, so the offset is relative to that channel's own 0x80000 register set (docs/mace-video.md, Driver access)"},
    {"type": "field", "disp": 200, "window": "MACEV", "offset": "0x100000", "label": "video record +200 (output channel)", "binaries": ["usr/cpu/sysgen/IP32boot/mvp.o"], "functions": ["mvptransfer_fix_output", "mvptransfer_cleardma", "mvpreg_initmace", "mvpreg_setpassthru", "mvpreg_syncpath_controls", "mvpreg_syncdevice_controls"], "loads": ["lw"], "why": "the controller record word at +200 is the output-channel pointer, 0xbf200000, which mvpreg_init stores at 0xbdc4 (docs/mace-video.md, Driver access)"},
